{"name":"Cake Batter","hex":"#f0eddb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich, sweet dessert food, typically made of flour, sugar, and eggs and baked in an oven, and often covered in icing.","A small mass of baked dough, especially a thin loaf from unleavened dough."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Coat (something) with a crust of solid material.","To form into a cake, or mass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cake"},{"term":"batter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit or strike violently and repeatedly.","To coat with batter (the food ingredient)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of flour and liquid (usually egg and milk), archetypically beaten (but in practice sometimes gently folded), used for baking (e.g. pancakes, cake, or Yorkshire pudding) or to coat food (e.g. fish) prior to frying.","A binge; a heavy drinking session."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Batter (cooking)","blocks":[{"text":"Batter is a flour mixture with liquid and other ingredients such as sugar, salt, egg, milk and leavening used for cooking. Batters are a pourable consistency that cannot be kneaded.\n Batter is most often used for cake, pancakes and as a coating for fried foods. It is also used for a variety of batter breads."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Batter_for_pancakes.jpg/330px-Batter_for_pancakes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batter_(cooking)","wikidata":"Q29493"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake","wikidata":"Q13276"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%8B%E0%B2%A7%E0%B2%BF_%E0%B2%B8%E0%B2%82%E0%B2%AA%E0%B2%A3%E0%B3%86.JPG/500px-%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%8B%E0%B2%A7%E0%B2%BF_%E0%B2%B8%E0%B2%82%E0%B2%AA%E0%B2%A3%E0%B3%86.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%8B%E0%B2%A7%E0%B2%BF_%E0%B2%B8%E0%B2%82%E0%B2%AA%E0%B2%A3%E0%B3%86.JPG/1280px-%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%8B%E0%B2%A7%E0%B2%BF_%E0%B2%B8%E0%B2%82%E0%B2%AA%E0%B2%A3%E0%B3%86.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%8B%E0%B2%A7%E0%B2%BF_%E0%B2%B8%E0%B2%82%E0%B2%AA%E0%B2%A3%E0%B3%86.JPG/500px-%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%8B%E0%B2%A7%E0%B2%BF_%E0%B2%B8%E0%B2%82%E0%B2%AA%E0%B2%A3%E0%B3%86.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wheat batter mixed with fenugreek leaves for making dosa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%8B%E0%B2%A7%E0%B2%BF_%E0%B2%B8%E0%B2%82%E0%B2%AA%E0%B2%A3%E0%B3%86.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Crepesteig_040.jpg/250px-Crepesteig_040.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dc/Crepesteig_040.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Crepesteig_040.jpg/250px-Crepesteig_040.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser